   9: # downscaling, mirror, horizontal/vertical bars
  10: 
  11: # description:
  12: # In the input you will see horizontal and vertical bars separating different regions/cells/partitions with each cell containing different colors, like a chessboard.
  13: # Each separated region has a single color.
  14: # To make the output, make a grid with one colored pixel for each region of the chessboard.
  15: # Finally mirror along the x-axis.
  16: 
  17: def main(input_grid):
  18:     """
  19:     Collapse a separator grid into one color per region, then mirror the compact grid left-to-right.
  20: 
  21:     Input structure:
  22:     - The input is divided into uniformly colored cells by horizontal and vertical separator bars.
  23:     - Each region between separators has a single color.
  24:     - The separator color forms a connected partition spanning the full canvas.
  25: 
  26:     Rule:
  27:     - Identify the separator color and extract all separator-delimited regions.
  28:     - Replace each region with one pixel of its region color, preserving row and column order.
  29:     - Mirror the compact region-color grid horizontally.
  30: 
  31:     Key insight:
  32:     - The large chessboard-like image is an enlarged region map; the final step is a left-right
  33:       reflection of that compressed map.
  34:     """
  35:     # Plan:
  36:     # 1. Determine the color of the separator between the regions
  37:     # 2. Extract all the regions separated by the separator color
